  "notes": "GAAP. Governmental receipts/disbursements from p4 Total Governmental Funds column; beginning/ending fund balance p4; ending_cash = governmental funds balance sheet cash and cash equivalents 1,990,364 (p3; restricted cash 389,836 separate). Interest/dividends 65,781 printed under Other Financing Sources below total receipts, recorded as receipt outside_printed_total. Net transfers (55,111) recorded as transfers_out. Transfer cross-check: governmental funds net -55,111 = business-type transfers +2,862 (p6) + internal service fund +52,249 (p6); no hidden transfers in spending lines. Budget schedule p8 prints gross transfers 11,140,495 in and out (shown as other financing; both detail_totals include them); it has only fund-level lines (budget schedule detail by fund, all funds incl. Electric, Water, Gas, Sewer, Internal service; budget_final only printed as totals 22,842,992 / 27,970,623). Detail totals are all-funds combined and mix fund types. Business-type from p6 total column (excludes internal service fund); beginning net position 40,160,892 as previously stated plus error correction -744,619 gives 55,265,427; no single printed total for business-type receipts/disbursements so computed. Business-type cash flows p7 total enterprise column; no noncapital financing section. Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position Total column (p1). Taxes combined line not breakable. Read pages 1-8 of 8 Recheck: the business-type 'Miscellaneous/ merchandise sales/ grants' line (p6) was split using the Statement of Activities (p2): capital grants and contributions 15,049,481 to intergovernmental/state aid (grantor not stated) and the 123,366 remainder to other (p2 shows other misc revenues 123,365; 1 rounding)."
